course: dictionary
lesson: 1665
title: Chlorophyll, the green helper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You may not know the word chlorophyll yet, but the words around it leave clues. «Chlorophyll is the green substance in plants that soaks up sunlight.» Green tells you its colour, and soaks up sunlight tells you it takes in light.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into a sentence. «Fungi cannot make their own food because they have no chlorophyll» becomes «because they have no green substance that soaks up sunlight». It still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Chlorophyll is also a clue to what happens in autumn. «In autumn trees stop making green chlorophyll, so hidden yellows and oranges show through.» When the green goes away, the other colours that were already in the leaf can be seen.
fact: Chlorophyll is the green substance in plants that soaks up sunlight.
fact: Plants use chlorophyll to make their own food from light, water and carbon dioxide.
fact: Chlorophyll is found in leaves, and it is why most leaves look green.
fact: «Fungi» cannot make their own food, because they have no chlorophyll.
fact: In autumn, chlorophyll breaks down, so yellow and red colours show in the leaves.
exercise: «Fungi cannot make their own food because they have no chlorophyll.» What does chlorophyll mean here? | The sound a leaf makes in the wind | A kind of soil | A type of mushroom | *The green substance in plants that soaks up sunlight
exercise: Plants use chlorophyll to make their own food from what? | Meat and fish | Only soil and rocks | *Light, water and carbon dioxide | Sweets and sugar bought from a shop
exercise: Why do most leaves look green? | *Because chlorophyll is in them | Because they are very old | Because they never grow | Because the sun paints them green
test: «In autumn trees stop making green chlorophyll.» What happens to chlorophyll in autumn? | It is eaten by animals | *It stops being made, so other colours show | It grows much bigger | It turns into water
test: Which sentence uses chlorophyll correctly? | Chlorophyll is a sound that leaves make. | Chlorophyll is the name of a red fungus. | *Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll. | Chlorophyll is a kind of animal.
exam: Plants use chlorophyll to soak up sunlight, and «chlorophyll» means which of these? | A red colour in autumn leaves | A type of fungus | *The green substance in plants that soaks up sunlight | A kind of soil
